[size=4][b]v2.1.0 — Skyrim 1.7.104 support[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]MFO supports Skyrim 1.7.104 (Steam).[/b] There is no Address Library for 1.7.104, so MFO carries its own table of game addresses for it inside the DLL. You install nothing extra. Every hook, address and game structure MFO uses was checked by hand against the 1.7.104 game files. Two game structures moved in 1.7.104 (the player and the script engine), and MFO handles both. Nobody has played MFO on 1.7.104 yet, so please report anything odd. Harbinger supports 1.7.104 in its own update. MFO.log names the game version and the table revision at startup.
[*][b]The engine can no longer raise skills MFO did not give a follower.[/b] Many follower mods use the game's auto-calc stats, which recompute skills from the class and level every time you level up. MFO already cancelled that for skills it manages. Every other skill kept drifting, which took Jesper's Light and Heavy Armor from 46 to 100. MFO now holds all 18 skills of a follower it manages at where they started, and its own points still raise them. A skill another mod trains on that follower is held back too. This follows the same setting that already cancels the engine's level-up gains.
[*][b]MFO now runs its engine features only on the game versions it was tested on.[/b] That is 1.6.1170, 1.5.97 and now 1.7.104. On any other version MFO says so in MFO.log at startup and keeps those features off, the Field Orders board included, instead of guessing.
[*][b]The menu is safer around other overlays and display changes.[/b] MFO now draws only on the game's own display and leaves any other one alone. If the game recreates its display, for example after a fullscreen or borderless switch, the menu turns itself off and closes so your controls are never locked with nothing on screen, and MFO.log says so clearly. If the menu cannot get a render target it says that too, with the error code. Nothing changes when all is well.
[*][b]Mage clothing is the most expensive piece in every slot.[/b] Without MEO installed, mages used to prefer school robes even with the school setting off. Now school robes only matter when the strict school option is on.
[*][b]A follower with a cast spell no longer drops their armor for clothes.[/b] MFO used to treat anyone with a cast rule as a mage and dress them in clothing only. Cicero got Arcane Pull and went back to the jester outfit. Now the class decides. A Melee or Ranged pick stays in armor. A Mage pick wears mage clothing. On Auto the highest base skill decides, and magic has to beat both melee and archery. MFO.log says which way each follower went.
[*][b]Followers no longer swap a worn helmet over and over.[/b] The sell code could mark a worn piece as surplus while the armor choice kept it. It then pulled the gem and the gem put it back on, 89 times for Cicero. The sell code now asks the armor choice first and leaves a worn piece it keeps alone.
[*][b]Class based health, magicka and stamina growth is now part of MFO itself.[/b] Every follower MFO manages grows by their class when they level, with or without the progression add-on. A Melee follower leans on health, a Ranged follower on stamina and a Mage on magicka. A follower on Auto gets a class too. MFO picks it from their gambits first, then their best combat skill, then their game class. Their growth also stays at your own rate, as it already did for progression followers. The add-on can still fine tune the split for its classes. A follower left on Auto is no longer marked as a fixed stat follower by mistake.
[*][b]Followers whose growth MFO never shaped keep what they have.[/b] A progression follower left on Auto, or without a class, was skipped before. MFO now takes their current health, magicka and stamina as their new starting point. Nothing is taken away. A wrong fixed stat mark on them is cleared. This happens once, for followers loaded from a save. A follower you enroll now keeps the usual protection on their first level jump.
[*][b]Going back to an older MFO loses this growth record.[/b] Versions 2.0.12 to 2.0.16 do not keep the new record for followers outside the progression add-on. Their next save drops it. Coming back to this version starts those followers fresh from their current stats.
[*][b]The menu can be translated without touching the DLL.[/b] Every word on the Field Orders board, the Followers and Gambits tabs, the Progression tab and the on-screen strip is now a named line in a text file. Make MFO_<LANGUAGE>.txt in Data/Interface/Translations/ (the same place and format MCM Helper uses) and the menu follows the game's language. A line you leave out stays English. MFO_ENGLISH.txt ships as the template and Docs/TRANSLATING.md explains the rest.
[*][b]Columns grow to fit longer words.[/b] A translated header or state no longer gets cut off in the Followers, Gambits and skill lists. Controller navigation works the same.
[*][b]Bad translation lines cannot break the game.[/b] A line with a missing or wrong {1} marker is skipped and MFO says so in MFO.log. The English text is used for that line.
[*][b]Archers pick the ranged weapon that has ammo.[/b] A follower with a bow and a crossbow now draws the one they can actually fire. A weapon with no matching ammo sorts below any that has some. If none has ammo, the old order stands. Perks that test for a bow or a crossbow in hand nudge the pick toward that kind. The vanilla Archery perks name the bow keyword that both kinds share, so they favour both alike. Modded guns work the same way, because the match comes from the weapon's own record. Loot and shopping then chase the ammo for the weapon they picked.
[*][b]The board and HUD hotkeys start empty.[/b] They no longer show a key in the MCM until you pick one. iBoardKey and iHudKey default to -1, and any value of 0 or less means no key. If your MCM still holds the old 0, MFO clears it to -1 once on upgrade. Pick a key and it stays.
[*][b]Followers make lockpicking sounds.[/b] While a follower works a lock you hear the pick at their position, and a pick snaps with the vanilla break sound at them for each pick they break. The sound gets quieter with distance, so a follower picking a lock far away is faint. MFO.esp carries its own copies of the two vanilla sounds for this, because the vanilla ones always play in your ears. They follow your sound effects volume.
[*][b]The Followers tab shows where retained followers are.[/b] A follower you are not currently travelling with now lists their current cell next to their name, or the location name if the cell has none.
[*][b]A healer's heal is no longer starved by their own attack spells.[/b] While a heal waits to start, it holds for up to 4 seconds. Attack rules ranked below it let go of the other hand, so the heal can start. Rules ranked above the heal still win. Normal play resumes the moment the heal fires.
[*][b]A retreating follower finishes the spell they are casting.[/b] The retreat waits a moment for a cast in flight, up to one and a half seconds, so a heal is no longer cut off mid-cast. When the retreat starts, any heal they had lined up is dropped at once instead of lingering.
[*][b]A retreating follower can still heal themself.[/b] While they fall back, a self heal rule keeps working once they are out of combat. They never heal others, attack or buff while retreating, and the walk is not disturbed.
[*][b]A follower no longer ends up wearing the outfit the game forces back on them.[/b] With Harbinger installed, followers in armor now ask for the best armor they own in every slot at once. An outfit piece the game puts back on them is no longer kept just because they are wearing it. A piece you put on them yourself still stays.
[*][b]The Logistics MCM page no longer shows a blank row without Legacy of the Dragonborn.[/b] The controls that only matter with that mod installed now sit at the end of the page, so nothing is left empty in the middle.
[/list]
